This comprehensive 7-day training program is engineered to maximize your specific equipment, accommodate your biomechanics as a taller athlete (1.91m), and precisely fit your 50-minute daily window.  
The resistance routines are structured to build hyper-functional core strength, muscular hypertrophy, and maximal strength while keeping your spine highly supported and joints protected. The daily 10-minute mobility cooldown is custom-designed to counter the specific tightness developed from cycling and racket sports, systematically working toward your goal of touching your head to your knees.

### **Weekly Training Split**

| Day | Focus Area | Primary Bench Angle | Intensity / Style |
| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |
| **Monday** | Push (Chest Focus) & Core | Flat / 30° Incline | Heavy Strength & Hypertrophy |
| **Tuesday** | Legs (Quad Focus) & Core | Flat | Stability & Hypertrophy |
| **Wednesday** | Pull (Back Focus) & Core | 45° Incline | Supported Strength & Posture |
| **Thursday** | Active Recovery & Deep Core | Flat | Isometric Holds & Bodyweight |
| **Friday** | Shoulders & Arms & Core | 90° Upright / Flat | Hypertrophy & Supersets |
| **Saturday** | Legs (Glute/Ham Focus) & Core | Flat | Hinge Mechanics & Control |
| **Sunday** | Active Recovery & Mobility | N/A | Light Flow & Extended Stretching |

### **Daily Workout Breakdowns (40 Minutes)**

*Pacing Rule: Stick strictly to the prescribed rest periods to complete the resistance portion in exactly 40 minutes. The first 3 minutes of every session serve as an active warm-up (jumping jacks, arm circles, unweighted squats).*

#### **Day 1: Push (Chest Focus) & Core**

* **1\. DB Bench Press (Flat Bench)**  
  * *Protocol:* 4 sets of 4-6 reps (Heaviest weight possible). Rest 90s.  
  * *Form Note:* Plant your long legs firmly. Keep shoulder blades retracted.  
* **2\. Superset:**  
  * **2A. Incline DB Fly (30° Bench):** 3 sets of 8-12 reps.  
  * **2B. Decline Push-Ups (Feet on flat bench):** 3 sets to failure.  
  * *Protocol:* Perform 2A, immediately do 2B, then rest 60s.  
* **3\. Weighted Bench Crunches (Decline or Flat)**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 12-15 reps with a single DB held at your chest. Rest 60s.  
  * *Form Note:* Control the descent; do not hyperextend the lower back.  
* **4\. Hollow Body Holds (Floor)**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 30-40 seconds. Rest 45s.

#### **Day 2: Legs (Quad Focus) & Core**

* **1\. DB Goblet Squats**  
  * *Protocol:* 4 sets of 8-12 reps. Rest 90s.  
  * *Form Note:* Elevate your heels slightly on weight plates if ankle mobility restricts depth.  
* **2\. Bulgarian Split Squats (Rear foot on flat bench)**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 8-10 reps per leg. Rest 60s.  
  * *Form Note:* Lean the torso forward slightly to engage the glutes and take the pressure off the front knee. Ensure your front knee tracks over your toes.  
* **3\. DB Reverse Lunges**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 10 reps per leg. Rest 60s.  
* **4\. Forearm Plank with DB Pull-Throughs**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 10 pulls per side. Rest 45s.

#### **Day 3: Pull (Back Focus) & Core**

* **1\. Chest-Supported DB Rows (45° Incline Bench)**  
  * *Protocol:* 4 sets of 6-8 reps. Rest 90s.  
  * *Form Note:* Lay face down on the bench. This entirely removes the lower back from the equation, allowing you to pull heavy weight safely.  
* **2\. Superset:**  
  * **2A. DB Pullovers (Lying perpendicular across flat bench):** 3 sets of 10-12 reps.  
  * **2B. Chest-Supported Reverse Flys (45° Incline):** 3 sets of 12-15 reps.  
  * *Protocol:* Perform 2A, immediately do 2B, then rest 60s.  
* **3\. Dead Bugs (Floor)**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 12 reps per side (slow and controlled). Rest 45s.

#### **Day 4: Active Recovery & Deep Core**

* **1\. Bodyweight Step-Ups (Onto flat bench)**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 15 reps per leg. Rest 45s.  
* **2\. Isometric Glute Bridges (Shoulders on bench)**  
  * *Protocol:* 4 sets of 45-second holds. Rest 45s.  
* **3\. Bird-Dogs**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 10 reps per side. Rest 30s.  
* **4\. Side Planks**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 45 seconds per side. Rest 30s.

#### **Day 5: Shoulders & Arms & Core**

* **1\. Seated DB Overhead Press (90° Upright Bench)**  
  * *Protocol:* 4 sets of 6-8 reps. Rest 90s. Keep your back pressed firmly into the pad.  
* **2\. Superset 1 (Shoulders):**  
  * **2A. DB Lateral Raises:** 3 sets of 10-12 reps.  
  * **2B. DB Front Raises:** 3 sets of 10-12 reps. Rest 60s.  
* **3\. Superset 2 (Arms):**  
  * **3A. DB Bicep Curls (Alternating):** 3 sets of 8-12 reps.  
  * **3B. DB Overhead Triceps Extension (Seated):** 3 sets of 8-12 reps. Rest 60s.  
* **4\. Russian Twists (Floor)**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 20 twists (holding one DB). Rest 45s.

#### **Day 6: Legs (Glute/Ham Focus) & Core**

* **1\. DB Romanian Deadlifts (RDLs)**  
  * *Protocol:* 4 sets of 8-10 reps. Rest 90s.  
  * *Form Note:* Push your hips straight back. Keep the dumbbells sliding down your thighs. Stop the moment your hamstrings are fully stretched; do not round your spine to go lower.  
* **2\. DB Hip Thrusts (Upper back on bench)**  
  * *Protocol:* 4 sets of 10-12 reps. Rest 60s.  
* **3\. Hamstring Walkouts (Lying on floor)**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 8 walkouts. Rest 45s.  
* **4\. Weighted Bench Crunches (Decline)**  
  * *Protocol:* 3 sets of 15 reps. Rest 45s.

#### **Day 7: Active Recovery & Mobility Focus**

* *Protocol:* Skip the dumbbells today. Spend 20 minutes performing bodyweight movements (unweighted squats, lunges, push-ups, planks) at a relaxed pace to encourage blood flow. Dedicate the remaining 30 minutes entirely to the mobility sequence below, holding each pose for double the usual time.

### **10-Minute Mobility & Stretching Block (Daily)**

This sequence runs exactly 10 minutes. Use a stopwatch. Transition smoothly from one movement to the next. The focus here is opening the thoracic spine (for tennis/paddle power), releasing the hips (from cycling), and lengthening the posterior chain to achieve your forward-fold milestone.  
**Minute 1-2: Thoracic Bench Extensions**

* Kneel on the floor facing the flat bench. Place your elbows on the bench pad, holding a light object (or just clasping hands) behind your head. Drop your chest toward the floor, stretching the lats and thoracic spine. Hold and take deep, diaphragmatic breaths.

**Minute 3-4: The World's Greatest Stretch (Dynamic)**

* Step into a deep lunge. Place the opposite hand on the floor. Reach the hand closest to your front leg down to your instep, then rotate that arm all the way up to the ceiling, opening your chest. Perform 5 slow rotations per side.

**Minute 5-6: 90/90 Hip Switches**

* Sit on the floor with both knees bent at 90 degrees, one leg internally rotated and the other externally rotated. Keeping your torso tall, pivot on your heels to flip your knees to the opposite side. Excellent for rotational hip mobility.

**Minute 7-8: Downward Dog to Cobra**

* Press into a Downward Dog, pedaling out your long legs to stretch the calves and hamstrings. Smoothly swoop down into a Cobra pose (hips on the floor, chest up), keeping your neck neutral. Alternate between the two positions.

**Minute 9-10: Progressive Seated Forward Fold (The Milestone Movement)**

* Sit with your legs straight out in front of you. Sit up as tall as possible, pulling your toes back toward your shins.  
* Inhale deeply, and as you exhale, hinge *only* at the hips (keep the lower back flat initially) and reach forward.  
* Once you hit your limit, gently allow the upper back to round, tucking your chin, aiming the top of your head toward your knees. Hold this static position for the final 60 seconds, using each exhale to sink a fraction of a millimeter deeper.